<title>USA: Roche confirms asthma-triggering protein.</title>
<headline>Roche confirms asthma-triggering protein.</headline>
<dateline>NUTLEY, N.J. 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Roche Holding Ltd subsidiary Hoffmann-La Roche Inc said Tuesday it has confirmed that a protein in the body that regulates inflammation is involved in triggering allergic asthma in animals.</p>
<p>The protein is known as tumor necrosis factor and proved to be a major causative agent in allergic lung inflammation during animal tests, the company said.</p>
<p>These results suggest that TNF inhibitors could become the next generation of drugs to treat asthma, the company said.</p>
</text>
